    "last_assistant_text": "The PoC triggered the vulnerability. The ASAN output confirms:\n\n- Double-free in `parser_leak_free` (gram.y:1866) → `parser_leak_init` → `init_parser`\n- First free at `sudoersparse` (gram.y:795) — that's the `free($$.runcwd)` in the `options chrootspec` rule\n- Original allocation in `fill_txt` via `sudoerslex` — the lexer allocated the WORD token string\n\nThe input `root ALL = CWD=/ CWD=/tmp ALL\\n` triggers the double-free by specifying two CWD options. The first CWD value gets freed when the second one is assigned, but the string remains on the parser leak list, causing it to be freed again during cleanup.",
